sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor EMP as Employee
    participant LH as Leave handler
    participant CAL as Working Calendar
    participant AE as Approval Engine
    participant NE as Notification Engine
    participant AL as Audit Log
    participant DB as Postgres
    actor MGR as Manager
    actor DIR as Director

    EMP->>LH: apply — 4 days, Casual
    activate LH

    Note over LH,DB: single transaction
    LH->>DB: SELECT balance FOR UPDATE
    Note right of DB: lock first, so two simultaneous<br/>requests cannot both pass validation
    LH->>CAL: working days between dates?
    CAL-->>LH: 4 — weekends and holidays excluded
    LH->>LH: is the start date past?
    Note right of LH: compared in the org's timezone,<br/>never the server clock
    LH->>DB: reserve 4 days
    Note right of DB: reserved on submission,<br/>released if rejected
    LH->>AE: approval_submit(leave_request, id, 4 days)
    activate AE
    AE->>DB: read approval_chains for this org
    DB-->>AE: L1 reporting manager · L2 if days over 3
    Note right of AE: the threshold is a row,<br/>not a line of code
    AE-->>LH: 2 levels required

    AE->>NE: approval.submitted
    NE->>MGR: email — 4 days awaiting approval
    AE->>AL: record
    deactivate LH

    MGR->>AE: approve
    AE->>NE: approval.decided
    NE->>DIR: email — escalated to you
    AE->>AL: record

    DIR->>AE: approve
    AE->>AL: record
    AE-->>LH: approval.completed — approved
    deactivate AE

    activate LH
    LH->>DB: reserved 4 becomes booked 4
    LH->>AL: record balance change
    LH->>NE: notify employee
    NE->>EMP: email — your leave is approved
    deactivate LH
